Subject: [PATCH] ksmbd-tools: persist subauthority on the data partition

The root image is read-only, so mountd cannot create its subauthority
file under /etc. Keep it alongside BananaOS settings on the data
partition so the server domain SID survives share restarts and reboots.

Refs: https://github.com/JorreFog/BananaLinux/issues/252
---
 include/tools.h | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/include/tools.h b/include/tools.h
--- a/include/tools.h
+++ b/include/tools.h
@@ -80,5 +80,8 @@
 #define PATH_PWDDB		SYSCONFDIR "/ksmbd/ksmbdpwd.db"
 #define PATH_SMBCONF		SYSCONFDIR "/ksmbd/ksmbd.conf"
-#define PATH_SUBAUTH		SYSCONFDIR "/ksmbd/ksmbd.subauth"
+#ifndef BANANA_DATA_DIR
+#define BANANA_DATA_DIR		"/data"
+#endif
+#define PATH_SUBAUTH		BANANA_DATA_DIR "/banana/ksmbd.subauth"
 #define PATH_LOCK		RUNSTATEDIR "/ksmbd.lock"
 #define PATH_FIFO		RUNSTATEDIR "/ksmbd.fifo"
